Keeps contents/resources/ in the repo while no kit is published.

A Field Kit is the second half of an episode, not a standalone page: the
video's closing lines point at it. So a kit's file lands here on the day its
video publishes, one at a time, and never before — a kit on the shelf ahead
of its video is a worksheet for a lesson nobody can take yet.

The folder itself is load-bearing and must not be deleted. It is the drop
target RESOURCES-CONTRACT.md guarantees ("adding a file here MUST be
sufficient to make the page exist"), and next.config.mjs traces it into the
serverless output. lib/resources.ts ignores every file that is not .md, so
this one is invisible to the site.
